      {
        "heading": "One doorbell, two brains",
        "accent": "cyan",
        "text": [
          "Lookout is a battery video doorbell built on the Cumulus IoT platform. Inside are two chips with opposite jobs: Sentry LP stays awake on 4 mW to hold WiFi, MQTT, and the motion sensor, while Vision HP — camera, encoder, neural nets — stays off until Sentry raises its interrupt line.",
          "Every diagram below is generated from one JSON spec and offers the same two views: ambient (everything animating) and a guided step-through. Tabs order the story from the doorbell's hero moment to what happens to your footage."
        ],
        "bullets": [
          "Sentry LP: always-on WiFi + MQTT session, PIR motion input, 4 mW idle",
          "Vision HP: camera, H.264 encoder, person/package classifier — normally powered off",
          "Cloud: Relay broker (MQTT/TLS), Pulse events, Herald push, Beam media, Vault clip store",
          "Line colors are protocols, and they draw the same in every diagram on this page"
        ]
      },
